<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:31:51 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Europe lifts sanctions against two Russians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe-lifts-sanctions-against-two-russians</link><description>
The EU has agreed to remove Russian billionaires Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman from its sanctions list, while extending restrictions on nearly 3,000 individuals and companies linked to Russia’s war in Ukraine for another three years. The decision came after difficult negotiations, as EU sanctions require unanimous approval from all 27 member states. Caroline Baum reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef89f844-b726-11f1-a45d-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-090753-090927-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef89f844-b726-11f1-a45d-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-090753-090927-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f54f87c6-b726-11f1-9009-9dbacafd3f48</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:26:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Azerbaijan pardons jailed Frenchman after EU lifts sanctions on Russian billionaire</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-azerbaijan-pardons-jailed-frenchman-after-eu-lifts-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs</link><description>
Azerbaijan's President ​Ilham Aliyev on Wednesday pardoned a ​French national imprisoned for espionage a day ​after ‌the ⁠EU lifted sanctions on a Russian billionaire.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3cf478e-b722-11f1-8a14-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26202440573121.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3cf478e-b722-11f1-8a14-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26202440573121.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62764d8e-b723-11f1-b74b-cddd5b8ec36a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 07:53:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3cf478e-b722-11f1-8a14-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26202440573121.jpg">© Ebrahim Noroozi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky says Ukraine is ready for an energy ceasefire with Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-zelensky-says-ukraine-is-ready-for-an-energy-ceasefire-with-russia</link><description>
On the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York on Tuesday, Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky told journalists that Kyiv is ready to halt strikes on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, with hopes to end the war before winter.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc1ad66-b6cd-11f1-9bea-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-22T185321Z-294428292-RC2IONAPQIAG-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY-ZELENSKIY-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc1ad66-b6cd-11f1-9bea-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-22T185321Z-294428292-RC2IONAPQIAG-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY-ZELENSKIY-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e66bd57e-b6cd-11f1-98a4-f92bcbda5e96</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:38:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fc1ad66-b6cd-11f1-9bea-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-22T185321Z-294428292-RC2IONAPQIAG-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY-ZELENSKIY-TRUMP.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Viral NATO video falsely framed as 'war propaganda' against Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/viral-nato-video-falsely-framed-as-war-propaganda-against-russia-1</link><description>
A viral NATO video is being falsely framed online as "war propaganda", with users accusing the Alliance of sharing a "promotional video" designed to prepare the public for imminent war with Russia. But the footage is not new: NATO published it in July 2024 for its 75th anniversary, and it's been stripped of its original context. The claim comes as European leaders warn of growing Russian hybrid threats, including alleged drone, cyber and sabotage activity. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2579b26c-b6c5-11f1-a667-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15120144666ab2e68f813325-23240503.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2579b26c-b6c5-11f1-a667-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15120144666ab2e68f813325-23240503.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08e656c8-b6c5-11f1-bcbe-6f1c77cf4e2d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:44:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How is the EU responding to record fuel prices?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-how-is-the-eu-approaching-record-fuel-prices</link><description>
Fuel prices have hit record highs across Europe in recent days, driven by soaring oil prices amid the war in the Middle East and Ukrainian strikes on Russian refineries. However, the scale of the increases, as well as the measures taken to address them, varies significantly from one EU country to another. Here’s why.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a788ff72-b69f-11f1-8f8a-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/7f50b136c93ac6ca88a6c611851705ecc2fc34fb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a788ff72-b69f-11f1-8f8a-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/7f50b136c93ac6ca88a6c611851705ecc2fc34fb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8d012bc-b69f-11f1-aae4-29f34d7893a5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:07:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a788ff72-b69f-11f1-8f8a-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/7f50b136c93ac6ca88a6c611851705ecc2fc34fb.jpg">© Alain Jocard, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ladin: Dolomites villages refuse to give up on ancient language</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-ladin-dolomites-villages-refuse-to-give-up-on-ancient-language</link><description>
Year after year, the mountains of the Dolomites become more popular with tourists. Amid millions of visitors, 30,000 inhabitants speak a language only they understand: Ladin, one of the oldest minority languages in Europe. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95696006-b5c4-11f1-bde2-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/TN-PANNEAU-ELENA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95696006-b5c4-11f1-bde2-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/TN-PANNEAU-ELENA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a14619fc-b29d-11f1-8799-01b081c75e09</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:30:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95696006-b5c4-11f1-bde2-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/TN-PANNEAU-ELENA.jpg">© ENTR</source><dc:creator>Elena POMPEI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Greenland agreement 'doesn't really give the US many more rights', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260922-greenland-agreement-doesn-t-really-give-the-us-many-more-rights-expert-says</link><description>
As the US, Denmark and Greenland itself sign an agreement on Greenland's security, we've been asking what difference it will actually make. Our expert says the deal won't really give the US many more rights, but that US President Donald Trump wanted to prevent at all costs the tiny risk of Greenland turning towards China. He adds that for Trump voters, if you inflate the risk, people will talk about it and see you're acting. We spoke in Perspective to Mikaa Blugeon-Mered, Senior Researcher on Hydrogen and Arctic Affairs at the Canada Research Chair in Clean Hydrogen at the University of Québec Trois Rivières.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/816fea02-b673-11f1-8b80-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8640513086ab25d97164463-88773820.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/816fea02-b673-11f1-8b80-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8640513086ab25d97164463-88773820.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">463b7f08-b666-11f1-b21b-7dfa233bdef3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:07:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>First New York, now Berlin: Why the left turn for major metropolises?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-first-new-york-now-berlin-why-the-left-turn-for-major-metropolises</link><description>
There's the inroads of the far right, but also the broader desire for change. Introducing Berlin's answer to Zohran Mamdani: Elif Eralp, who led the far-left Die Linke party's historic win in Sunday's municipal elections in Berlin. We ask if the 45-year-old daughter of Turkish political exiles can push through her promises of rent freezes and nationalisation of private real estate companies. Just like in New York last year, affordable housing was a hot-button issue. It didn't hurt that her party ran a social media-savvy campaign.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f7feb3a-b5e8-11f1-9cad-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T165634Z-360619873-RC24NNADN54W-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-LINKE-REACTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f7feb3a-b5e8-11f1-9cad-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T165634Z-360619873-RC24NNADN54W-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-LINKE-REACTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b7df62c8-b5e4-11f1-b1d9-f14263dd641d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:56:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK and US make first-ever torpedo test from uncrewed vessel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-uk-and-us-make-first-ever-torpedo-test-from-uncrewed-vessel</link><description>
The United Kingdom and the United States have for the first time test-fired a torpedo from an uncrewed underwater vessel, the UK government said Monday, marking a step forward in AUKUS efforts to develop autonomous naval technology.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79eb4d1c-b62d-11f1-81e1-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-37AZ22V.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79eb4d1c-b62d-11f1-81e1-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-37AZ22V.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd9f6142-b62d-11f1-86ec-57d3f37dfb46</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 02:33:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79eb4d1c-b62d-11f1-81e1-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/000-37AZ22V.jpg">© Oli Scarff, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU to lift sanctions on Russian oligarchs Usmanov, Fridman</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260922-eu-fails-to-agree-on-lifting-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs</link><description>
EU countries on Tuesday agreed a compromise deal to prolong sanctions on Russia that will see oligarchs Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman removed from the blacklist, diplomats said. Ukraine called the EU’s delisting of Usmanov and Fridman “shameful” and urged national sanctions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0d164d12-e0cd-11f0-83d4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24085394195061.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0d164d12-e0cd-11f0-83d4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24085394195061.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f34a0c86-b62b-11f1-a1f8-835403065098</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 02:18:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0d164d12-e0cd-11f0-83d4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24085394195061.jpg">© Virginia Mayo, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Brigitte Bardot's personal possessions sell for nearly €1 million at Paris auction</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-bardot-auction-in-paris-fetches-nearly-one-million-euros</link><description>
An auction of the personal belongings of French screen icon Brigitte Bardot fetched nearly €1 million in Paris on Monday, with the sale featuring hundreds of personal objects ranging from sunglasses to furniture.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9522478-b5fe-11f1-96c6-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/f8c26cefcb9d0e76622ca3dfe0b0c216723429be.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9522478-b5fe-11f1-96c6-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/f8c26cefcb9d0e76622ca3dfe0b0c216723429be.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba46bc22-b5fe-11f1-8e43-71cf669b8034</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 20:55:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b9522478-b5fe-11f1-96c6-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/f8c26cefcb9d0e76622ca3dfe0b0c216723429be.jpg">© Charlotte Siemon, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Bayeux Tapestry craze prompts photo ban at British Museum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-bayeux-tapestry-craze-prompts-photo-ban-at-british-museum</link><description>
The British Museum said on Monday that it has banned people from taking photos of the Bayeux Tapestry to prevent crowds from backing up at the new exhibit. The 1,000-year-old artwork is on display in the UK after an unprecedented loan from France, and tickets are sold out until December 31.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f188137c-b5e3-11f1-aa9d-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-10T113528Z-983900571-RC2AGNAOY4FI-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-FRANCE-BAYEUX-TAPESTRY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f188137c-b5e3-11f1-aa9d-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-10T113528Z-983900571-RC2AGNAOY4FI-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-FRANCE-BAYEUX-TAPESTRY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6c7c4f96-b5d3-11f1-8fbe-2da3b455fe3b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:45:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f188137c-b5e3-11f1-aa9d-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-10T113528Z-983900571-RC2AGNAOY4FI-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-FRANCE-BAYEUX-TAPESTRY.jpg">© Toby Melville, Reuters </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU fines Google €403 million for improperly using location data</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-eu-fines-google-%E2%82%AC403-million-for-improperly-using-location-data</link><description>
Ireland, on behalf of the European Union, said Monday it had fined Google €403 million for improperly using users' location data between May 2018 and February 2020. However, the eight-year delay drew some criticism, as the European Consumer Organisation said that "can be as harmful as no enforcement at all". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b61a184-b5ca-11f1-9736-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26264428506639.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b61a184-b5ca-11f1-9736-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26264428506639.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ad44e78-b5ca-11f1-8fe0-81a66dccc7e9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 15:05:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b61a184-b5ca-11f1-9736-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26264428506639.jpg">©  Jeff Chiu, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany's Merz vows to hold ruling coalition together after election gains by far right, hard left</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-germany-merz-vows-to-keep-ruling-coalition-together-after-election-defeats</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz vowed Monday to keep his ruling coalition of the centre-right CDU and centre-left SPD together for the sake of the country's "democratic future", after both the far right and hard left made big gains in Germany's state elections on Sunday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/665876ee-b5ba-11f1-a538-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-21T121747Z-1525533954-RC2ONNAVETOZ-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-CDU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/665876ee-b5ba-11f1-a538-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-21T121747Z-1525533954-RC2ONNAVETOZ-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-CDU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b17f9e-b5b8-11f1-a3b5-9bc8026fa260</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:02:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/665876ee-b5ba-11f1-a538-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-21T121747Z-1525533954-RC2ONNAVETOZ-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-CDU.jpg">© Fabrizio Bensch, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Five takeaways from Germany's regional elections after far-right gains</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-five-takeaways-from-germany-s-regional-elections-after-far-right-gains</link><description>
Sunday's elections in two German states resulted in the defeat of the country's ruling CDU, a result described as a “disaster” by Chancellor Friedrich Merz. In Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, in the northeast of the country, the far-right AfD became the strongest party while the hard-left Die Linke led the polls in Berlin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b17dcb9e-b50e-11f1-b45e-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263254996213.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b17dcb9e-b50e-11f1-b45e-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263254996213.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8221011c-b57d-11f1-a8ec-0d0fe2c34e2f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 06:47:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b17dcb9e-b50e-11f1-b45e-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263254996213.jpg">© Jens Battner, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine slams EU's 'unacceptable' move to lift sanctions on two Russian oligarchs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260921-live-united-russia-dominates-in-elections-moscow-vows-revenge-after-massive-drone-attack</link><description>
Ukrainian Foreign Minister Andriy Sybiga on Monday called the removal of two Russian oligarchs from the European Union's sanctions list "unacceptable". Earlier, the bloc's envoys agreed to lift sanctions on businessmen Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman, as long as no EU government objected. Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d1c3d2e-b108-11ec-8922-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/310322-ousmanov-poutine-m.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d1c3d2e-b108-11ec-8922-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/310322-ousmanov-poutine-m.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24166f94-b564-11f1-8cc5-ebecccd8b3d0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:28:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d1c3d2e-b108-11ec-8922-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/310322-ousmanov-poutine-m.jpg">© Mikhail Klimentyev, AP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia's ruling party on track to win election after Ukraine's drone attacks on Moscow</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-russia-s-ruling-party-on-track-to-win-election-after-ukraine-s-drone-attacks-on-moscow</link><description>
Russia's ruling United Russia party on Sunday was projected to win the country's tightly controlled parliamentary elections, according to exit polls. Ukraine launched a massive drone attack on Moscow, killing three people, said city officials, on the third and final day of Russia's wartime vote. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90be9e84-b52b-11f1-b600-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263602850279.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90be9e84-b52b-11f1-b600-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263602850279.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d88ce52c-b52b-11f1-9b1b-cf12b455aafb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:14:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/90be9e84-b52b-11f1-b600-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263602850279.jpg">© Alexander Zemlianichenko, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Exit polls show 'disaster' for Merz' CDU party in two state elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/exit-polls-show-disaster-for-merz-cdu-party-in-two-state-elections</link><description>
Germans headed to the polls today in two state elections - in Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. Exit polls suggest a dramatic loss for the Chancellor Freidrich Mertz's Christian Democratic Union party. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Berlin, Jörg Taszman.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8707b430-b511-11f1-99f9-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-180658-181009-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8707b430-b511-11f1-99f9-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-180658-181009-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d0a6170-b511-11f1-be8f-db25dee039d2</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:54:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany’s Merz admits ‘disaster’ in state elections, vows to press ahead with reforms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-strong-gains-in-two-state-elections</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz on Sunday described his CDU party's heavy losses in two regional elections as a "disaster", but vowed to push ahead with a reform drive. The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party took first place in ​the northeastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, exit polls showed, and also gained in strength in another election in Berlin. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/010c050e-b5b4-11f1-985c-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/Merz-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/010c050e-b5b4-11f1-985c-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/Merz-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf2c6998-b50e-11f1-9061-b5b40a7a4c80</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:23:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/010c050e-b5b4-11f1-985c-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/Merz-EN.jpg">© Screen grab, France 24</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>AfD threatens fresh blow to Merz: Two German states hold key vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/afd-threatens-fresh-blow-to-merz-two-german-states-hold-key-vote</link><description>
Two German states are heading to the polls today – in Berlin and the state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. The far-right AfD party is expected to make further gains after securing a historic win in Saxony-Anhalt two weeks ago, though it has no realistic path to power in Berlin. Sunday's vote is a key test for Chancellor Friedrich Merz, one that could determine whether he can hold on to power. Details with Jamie Smith-Maillet, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46b47c8c-b503-11f1-b65c-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1450590606aaff3cdae6eb7-21030001.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46b47c8c-b503-11f1-b65c-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1450590606aaff3cdae6eb7-21030001.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">572a8de6-b502-11f1-896e-c5a169333d19</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:56:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Putin's party wins record number of parliamentary seats in first vote since 2022 invasion of Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-putin-s-party-set-to-retain-power-after-russia-vote-hit-by-cyberattacks-drones</link><description>
The main Kremlin party enlarged its majority with a record 355 seats in parliament, Russian election officials said Monday, after a carefully orchestrated ballot that excluded most opposition candidates helped the government maintain its tight grip on power. The election was the first since Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa7eac32-b59f-11f1-9df4-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/New-photo-Russia.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa7eac32-b59f-11f1-9df4-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/New-photo-Russia.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">234b8124-b502-11f1-a754-5f628a393564</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:47:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aa7eac32-b59f-11f1-9df4-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/New-photo-Russia.jpg">© Anastasia Barashkova, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine fires over 1,000 drones at Russia in "largest ever" attack on Moscow</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-fires-over-1-000-drones-at-russia-in-largest-ever-attack-on-moscow</link><description>
Russia is completing its three-day vote for the Duma this Sunday – the first since its large-scale invasion of Ukraine. The election was organised for the first time also in the Ukrainian regions occupied by Russia, and it was marked by Ukrainian drone strikes at various areas - mainly Moscow. Details by Shirli Sitbon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1124f9e-b501-11f1-bf2f-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-160125-160258-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1124f9e-b501-11f1-bf2f-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-160125-160258-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6b61282-b501-11f1-b8a9-5f628a393564</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:46:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany: Could regional polls force Friedrich Merz to step down?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/germany-could-regional-polls-froce-friedrich-merz-to-step-down</link><description>
Polling is underway in the German capital Berlin and the largely rural state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania for regional elections. Both elections are seen as a test for Germany's centre-right Chancellor Friedrich Merz. He has already scheduled a crisis meeting and decided to skip this week's UN General Assembly to deal with the potential fallout. Could he be forced to step down based on the election’s results? Details and analysis by Yann Wernert, senior policy fellow at the Jacques Delors Centre in Berlin.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7241ef7c-b4dd-11f1-a7e3-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-090118-091249-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7241ef7c-b4dd-11f1-a7e3-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-090118-091249-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78326d26-b4dd-11f1-90d4-2dedec0bd379</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:26:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine hits Russia with major drone attack, targeting refinery</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hits-russia-with-major-drone-attack-targetting-refinery</link><description>
In Russia, voters are on the third and final day of casting ballots in the country's first wartime parliamentary election. Despite the voting however, Ukraine carried out what Moscow described as the "largest ever" drone attack on the Russian capital. Kyiv reportedly fired over 1.000 drones at the country, leaving two dead in the Moscow region and inflicting damage upon an oil refinery. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fbde97c-b4be-11f1-b2c6-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T042905Z-1824787393-RC2QMNA5QBAK-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-REFINERY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7fbde97c-b4be-11f1-b2c6-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T042905Z-1824787393-RC2QMNA5QBAK-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-RUSSIA-REFINERY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b738272-b4db-11f1-924e-53fa25c99ab7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:24:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US and Denmark reach Greenland security deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal</link><description>
The US and Denmark have announced a deal on Greenland's security, resolving a diplomatic dispute sparked by President Donald Trump when he threatened to seize the semi-autonomous territory. The exact terms of the deal remain uncertain but it seems Denmark will maintain its sovereignty while the US will be able to develop a significant military presence on the island, and ban their adversaries from building their own bases on the island. Details by Charlotte Hughes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63667182-b4d6-11f1-8b04-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-081031-081205-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63667182-b4d6-11f1-8b04-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260920-081031-081205-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">691519ee-b4d6-11f1-ae1f-b37ea51a3338</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:40:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will German's far right party AfD win over two more regions?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/will-german-s-far-right-party-afd-win-over-two-more-regions</link><description>
Two weeks after the far-right AfD won its first major regional election in Germany, two more eastern states vote this Sunday. Polls have just opened in the capital, Berlin, and the largely rural state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Berlin, Jörg Taszman.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7190e544-b4d6-11f1-bbc5-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T154724Z-1958111571-RC23LNAVC6LP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-MERZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7190e544-b4d6-11f1-bbc5-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T154724Z-1958111571-RC23LNAVC6LP-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-MERZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d61c38a4-b4d3-11f1-bc01-f962a54c6b9f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 09:35:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia vows to ‘intensify’ strikes on Kyiv after Ukraine’s election-day drone attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-live-russian-election-enters-final-day-in-shadow-of-war-in-ukraine</link><description>
Russia on Sunday vowed to "intensify" its strikes on Kyiv in response to a massive wave of Ukrainian drone attacks on Moscow on the third and final day of voting in Russia’s first wartime parliamentary elections. The drone strikes, described as the “largest ever” attack on the Russian capital, killed three people and damaged  part of an oil refinery. Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad29a23c-b4e8-11f1-bbcc-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T080755Z-1641565567-RC2VMNAVR4TB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-MOSCOW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad29a23c-b4e8-11f1-bbcc-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T080755Z-1641565567-RC2VMNAVR4TB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-MOSCOW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a6beeb8-b4b2-11f1-8711-b95734b6451c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 05:16:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad29a23c-b4e8-11f1-bbcc-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T080755Z-1641565567-RC2VMNAVR4TB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-MOSCOW.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Merz under pressure as two more German states hold elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-germans-vote-in-elections-threatening-fresh-blow-to-merz</link><description>
Germans began voting Sunday in two closely watched state elections that could deliver fresh gains for the far-right and far-left, piling pressure on Chancellor Friedrich Merz as he struggles with low approval ratings and tensions within his governing coalition.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815009e2-b4bd-11f1-b531-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263230529590.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815009e2-b4bd-11f1-b531-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263230529590.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1996492c-b492-11f1-ac6a-af9a874d6e90</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 01:25:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/815009e2-b4bd-11f1-b531-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263230529590.jpg">© Markus Schreiber, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Greenland Deal: Greenland: A Trump Win or Danish Masterclass?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260919-greenland-deal-greenland-a-trump-win-or-danish-masterclass</link><description>
Is there a resolution on Greenland? President Trump’s pressure campaign began in December 2024, right after he won re-election, when he began talking about the need for US ownership and control of the semi-autonomous Danish territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d23c3d0-b44d-11f1-bf20-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/MILANO-CORTINA-000-97EH8CM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d23c3d0-b44d-11f1-bf20-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/MILANO-CORTINA-000-97EH8CM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06fcd610-b44b-11f1-bc77-371511a1c13c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:37:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany braces for key state elections where far right party AfD seeks another breakthrough</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/germany-braces-for-key-state-elections-where-far-right-party-afd-seeks-another-breakthrough</link><description>
Germany is gearing up for two more pivotal state elections on Sunday: in the capital Berlin and in the largely rural region of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. All eyes are on the far-right AfD, which after recording its best ever result in the recent Saxony-Anhalt elections, is hoping to once again make sweeping gains. The anti-immigration party's surging popularity is proving challenging for Chancellor Friedrich Merz and both elections are expected to further test his leadership. Story by Eliza Herbert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5936ae04-b43e-11f1-82e1-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-170853-171035-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5936ae04-b43e-11f1-82e1-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-170853-171035-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5e53ee2e-b43e-11f1-b651-a34c468dece1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:28:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
